    "text": "To determine how many kids are still awake, we will follow the steps outlined in the problem:\n\n1. **Initial number of kids**: There are 20 kids in preschool.\n\n2. **Kids who fall asleep in the first 5 minutes**: \n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{2} \\text{ of the kids} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 20 = 10 \\text{ kids}\n   \\]\n   So, after 5 minutes, the number of kids still awake is:\n   \\[\n   20 - 10 = 10 \\text{ kids}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Kids who fall asleep in the next 5 minutes**: \n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{2} \\text{ of the remaining kids} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 = 5 \\text{ kids}\n   \\]\n   So, after another 5 minutes, the number of kids still awake is:\n   \\[\n   10 - 5 = 5 \\text{ kids}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of kids still awake is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).",
